[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | E17 | `max_size_frame` | out-of-range "enum-like" integer passed for `bitdepth` (values that are not real FLAC depths: 1, 7, 33, 64, 0xFFFF, 0x80000000) | no rejection; only the `== 32` test matters, arithmetic proceeds | `err_e17_out_of_range_bitdepth_values` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Notes on C semantics that the rows above pin down
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `uint32_t` is `unsigned int` on this ABI (verified: `sizeof(unsigned) == 4`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and `__builtin_types_compatible_p(uint32_t, unsigned) == 1`), so the integer
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   promotions do **not** widen any operand to `int`. Every operation is done in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `unsigned int` and therefore wraps modulo 2^32 with fully defined behaviour —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   there is no signed-overflow UB to worry about, and equally no trap for the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Rust to reproduce.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `(channels != 2)`, `(channels == 2)`, `(bitdepth != 32)` are C `int`s valued
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   0 or 1, converted to `unsigned int` in the surrounding multiplications.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * The stray unary `+` in `+7` is a no-op; the addend is 7.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `/ 8` on an unsigned value truncates toward zero and cannot trap.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
