[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `max_size_frame` has no runtime option struct, no global state, no flags, and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `#ifdef`s. Its entire "configuration" is carried by the three value arguments,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and the code branches on exactly three predicates:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | predicate in C | states | effect |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|----------------|--------|--------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | A. channel mode | `channels != 2` / `channels == 2` | stereo (`== 2`) vs non-stereo (`!= 2`) | selects which of the three bit-count terms contribute. Non-stereo: term1 only. Stereo: term2 + term3 only. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | B. depth mode | `bitdepth != 32` | `bitdepth == 32` vs `bitdepth != 32` | only read inside term3, i.e. only observable when `channels == 2`. Adds a `+1` per-sample correction unless the depth is exactly 32. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C. input shape | (no predicate — value magnitude) | zero / one / small / typical / large / 2^32-wrapping | selects whether the wrapping multiplies and the `+7` stay in range or overflow, and whether `/ 8` truncates. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Cross-product = 2 (A) x 2 (B) x shape classes, pruned to the combinations the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m code actually treats differently. Note that B is *dead* when `channels != 2`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (the `bitdepth != 32` result is multiplied by `(channels == 2)` = 0), so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `channels != 2` rows must still be tested at both depth states to confirm the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rust also treats it as dead rather than applying the correction.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Public entry points
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is exactly one public entry point, and it is simultaneously the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lowest-level and the highest-level one — the header declares no other function,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and `lib.c` defines no internal helpers. There is no convenience wrapper layer
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m to bypass and no composed pipeline to drive; the "full operation end to end" is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m this single call. Every row below therefore calls `max_size_frame` directly
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m through the `.so` export in both libraries.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is also no binary/driver target: `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` declares only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `add_library(... SHARED src/lib.c)`, so the stdout-comparison item of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m completion gate is not applicable.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
